tags: pci-model, pci

A fact of a device on PCI: its model, as the PCI vendor id and device id.

The value is the two ids as 4 lowercase hexadecimal digits each, separated by ":".
Example: 10de:2330. A rate of a device can use this fact as its scope.

An absent fact: the node gives no PCI model. The node is bound: it attests the fact.

